nning."]}, "overview": "Senator Cory Booker seeks another term against Republican Justin Murphy, a little-funded challenger, with minor-party and independent candidates also on the ballot. No public general-election polling is available, so the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets, all of which point the same direction.\n\nBooker holds a massive financial edge, with $23 million on hand versus roughly a hundred dollars for Murphy, and no outside groups are spending against him. All ten expert raters call the race Solid or Safe D, and prediction markets price a Booker win at 96 to 99 percent. The debates in October drew attention but no sign of a competitive race. New Jersey's Democratic lean and the incumbent's profile make an upset highly unlikely.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 16.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9897, "margin": 16.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9901, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.991, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9894, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9935, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9868, "margin": 16.6}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9884, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9896, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.991, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": 